  "cooked": "<p>This is now being discussed in this PR:</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox githubpullrequest\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/pull/2340\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/pull/2340\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">github.com/bitcoin/bips</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"github-row\" data-github-private-repo=\"false\">\n\n\n\n    <div class=\"github-icon-container\" title=\"Pull Request\">\n      <svg width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"github-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M11 11.28V5c-.03-.78-.34-1.47-.94-2.06C9.46 2.35 8.78 2.03 8 2H7V0L4 3l3 3V4h1c.27.02.48.11.69.31.21.2.3.42.31.69v6.28A1.993 1.993 0 0 0 10 15a1.993 1.993 0 0 0 1-3.72zm-1 2.92c-.66 0-1.2-.55-1.2-1.2 0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2 0 .65-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2zM4 3c0-1.11-.89-2-2-2a1.993 1.993 0 0 0-1 3.72v6.56A1.993 1.993 0 0 0 2 15a1.993 1.993 0 0 0 1-3.72V4.72c.59-.34 1-.98 1-1.72zm-.8 10c0 .66-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2-.65 0-1.2-.55-1.2-1.2 0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2zM2 4.2C1.34 4.2.8 3.65.8 3c0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2 0 .65-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2z\"></path></svg>\n    </div>\n\n  <div class=\"github-info-container\">\n\n\n\n      <h4>\n        <a href=\"https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/pull/2340\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">BIP395: Unspendable Internal Keys for Wallet Policies (#2340)</a>\n      </h4>\n\n    <div class=\"branches\">\n      <code>master</code> \u2190 <code>bitryonix:bip-unspendable-internal-keys</code>\n    </div>\n\n      <div class=\"github-info\">\n        <div class=\"date\">\n          opened <span class=\"discourse-local-date\" data-format=\"ll\" data-date=\"2026-11-01\" data-time=\"06:43:15\" data-timezone=\"UTC\">06:43AM - 01 Nov 26 UTC</span>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"user\">\n          <a href=\"https://github.com/2099999997690000\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">\n            <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://delvingbitcoin.org/uploads/default/original/2X/0/0167cc976067227d9abccf0f508bcc83e7f1c700.jpeg\" class=\"onebox-avatar-inline\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" data-dominant-color=\"92435F\">\n            2099999997690000\n          </a>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"lines\" title=\"13 commits changed 18 files with 5921 additions and 0 deletions\">\n          <a href=\"https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/pull/2340/files\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">\n            <span class=\"added\">+5921</span>\n            <span class=\"removed\">-0</span>\n          </a>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n  <div class=\"github-row\">\n    <p class=\"github-body-container\">This proposes `_` as an unspendable Taproot internal-key placeholder in wallet p<span class=\"show-more-container\"><a href=\"https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/pull/2340\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\" class=\"show-more\">\u2026</a></span><span class=\"excerpt hidden\">olicies. Wallets and signers can reproduce the internal key from the policy and derivation path, without keeping a separate random tweak.\n\nThe construction uses the BIP 341 NUMS point as the public key of a synthetic BIP 32 root. Its chain code commits to the normalized policy, including both the keys and the policy structure. Child keys are then derived using unhardened BIP 32 derivation.\n\nThis builds on the [Delving discussion](https://delvingbitcoin.org/t/unspendable-keys-in-descriptors/304) and the earlier work in #1746. I shared an earlier draft on the [Bitcoin Development Mailing List](https://groups.google.com/g/bitcoindev/c/se3TkNnbno4).\n\nI've included a Python reference implementation, fixed JSON test vectors, and instructions for running the checks. All 21 offline tests pass, and the export and derivation cross-check passes all 20 cases against Bitcoin Core 31.0.</span></p>\n  </div>\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n",
